schema: "0.4"
id: sem-md-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-md
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-md>` element — a block whose content
    is authored as Markdown and rendered to HTML in the browser: a table
    above all, then headings, lists, emphasis, links, code and quotes. One
    example page per display mode the element provides, rendered in the
    minimal-tech theme on a dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface #1e293b,
    fg #e2e8f0, accent violet #7c5cff). TWO stacked example pages, each one
    authored Markdown block inside a slim browser-chrome frame, labeled with
    a small mono uppercase caption. The same authored block on both pages: a
    three-column token-lifetime GFM table (Token / Lifetime / Rotates;
    columns aligned left / right / center; rows "access · 15 min · no" and
    "refresh · 30 days · yes").

    Page 1 — caption "RENDERED (default)". A hairline #334155 rounded card
    (12px radius). A slim chrome row across the top: the label "Token
    lifetimes" in 600-weight sans on the left; on the right two small
    outlined buttons, "Markdown" (the toggle, unpressed) and "Copy". Below
    the chrome, the Markdown rendered as a real HTML table: small-caps
    column headers TOKEN, LIFETIME, ROTATES; the first column left-aligned,
    the second right-aligned, the third centered, exactly as the delimiter
    row asks; hairline row rules, no zebra striping. Beneath the Copy button
    a tiny status text "Copied" in muted foreground — the copy confirmation,
    shown once to demonstrate the feedback. The table reads as clean
    typographic HTML; no pipes, no backticks, no monospace anywhere in the
    table body.

    Page 2 — caption "RAW". The identical chrome row, but the "Markdown"
    toggle is now pressed (violet outline, accent-tinted) and the body has
    swapped to the raw view: the same table as its pipe-delimited Markdown
    source in a monospace face, left-aligned, every pipe and delimiter dash
    visible, content unchanged from the authored block (byte-identical,
    common indent stripped). A second slim chrome row for the code fence
    carries two small buttons, "Copy" and "Wrap", right-aligned. The raw
    view reads as readable preformatted text on the same dark card — a
    machine-faithful round trip of exactly what page 1 rendered.

    Typography: clean system sans (Inter-like) for chrome and rendered
    table, monospace only on the raw page, 16px body, 1.6 line height,
    generous margins. No extra chrome, no decorative icons, no pointer
    cursors drawn as graphics.
  negative: >
    pipes or backticks visible on the rendered page; a rendered HTML table
    on the raw page; line numbers in the raw fence; different content
    between the two pages; the block drawn as a form control, modal or
    floating panel; more than two example pages; light background; neon
    glow; drop shadows on text; lorem ipsum as table content; the status
    text rendered as a toast or alert bubble.
  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    (violet #7c5cff) palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155
    borders, generous negative space. Looks like a panel from a
    design-system guide.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-md/sem-md-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-md/sem-md-primary-render-markdown-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-md/sem-md-primary-source-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-md-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: rendered
      label: "RENDERED (default)"
      must_show:
        - the authored table as a real HTML table (thead, small-caps headers,
          per-column alignment honoured — left / right / center)
        - chrome row with the label left and unpressed "Markdown" toggle plus
          "Copy" button right; a small muted "Copied" status beside Copy
        - no Markdown syntax characters anywhere in the table body
      must_never:
        - show pipes, backticks or monospace glyphs in the rendered table
        - render the table as preformatted text
        - occlude, blur or dim any cell content
    - id: raw
      label: "RAW"
      must_show:
        - the same table as its pipe-delimited Markdown source in monospace,
          byte-identical content, indentation stripped
        - the "Markdown" toggle pressed (violet accent state)
        - a fence chrome row with "Copy" and "Wrap" buttons
      must_never:
        - show a rendered HTML table on this page
        - alter, truncate or reword the Markdown between pages
        - show line numbers in the fence

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    rendered-fidelity:
      weight: 0.4
      description: >
        Page 1 reads as clean typographic HTML — real table semantics,
        alignment honoured, chrome with label, toggle, Copy and a small
        "Copied" status.
      fail_signals:
        - pipes or backticks on the rendered page
        - alignment ignored (all columns flush left)
        - status drawn as a toast, modal or floating bubble
    raw-fidelity:
      weight: 0.3
      description: >
        Page 2 shows the identical content as its Markdown source:
        monospace, pipes intact, pressed toggle, fence Copy/Wrap chrome.
      fail_signals:
        - raw page shows a rendered table
        - source text differs from page 1's table
        - line numbers present in the fence
    round-trip-parity:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        The two pages carry the same token-lifetime table — same columns,
        same rows, only the representation changes.
      fail_signals:
        - different rows, columns or wording between pages
        - more or fewer than two labeled pages
    theme-fidelity:
      weight: 0.1
      description: >
        Dark minimal-tech palette (#0f172a bg, #7c5cff accent), hairline
        borders, mono uppercase captions, browser-chrome frames.
      fail_signals:
        - light background or multiple accent hues
        - watermark, lorem ipsum, decorative noise
  reject_if:
    - the rendered page shows raw Markdown syntax
    - the raw page shows a rendered HTML table
    - the two pages show different table content
